---
import { brand } from "@tandoor/brand";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title={`Terms of Service | ${brand.name}`}
  description="Terms for using Tandoor, a private Telegram agent available by invitation."
  currentPage="terms"
>
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="prose-page brand-prose">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: November 14, 2026</p>

    <p>
      Tandoor is a private Telegram agent made available to invited users.
      By using it, you agree to these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Use of the Service</h2>
    <p>
      Use Tandoor only if you are authorized to access it. You are
      responsible for your instructions, the accounts you connect, and
      ensuring you have permission to access or change the information
      involved in a request.
    </p>

    <h2>Connected Accounts and Agent Actions</h2>
    <p>
      When you connect Google or another service, Tandoor can use the
      permissions you grant to carry out your requests. Depending on your
      instructions, the agent may read, create, send, update, or delete
      information. Review important actions and results. Agent responses
      can be incomplete or incorrect.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for reviewing messages and files you share in
      Telegram. Tandoor handles private chats only; group chats are not
      supported.
    </p>

    <h2>Third Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      Tandoor depends on Telegram, Google, and AI model providers. Their
      services are governed by their own terms and may change or become
      unavailable.
    </p>

    <h2>Availability and Changes</h2>
    <p>
      Tandoor is an early personal project and is provided without a
      promise of uninterrupted availability. The operator may change,
      suspend, or discontinue access to the service.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms can be sent to{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${brand.contactEmail}`}>{brand.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
